A||N||10||AusFiero||What to do with a burnt Fiero.||||7||
Z||000000||AusFiero||11-27-2001||06:55 AM||||Well as most would know my Fiero got burnt in a fire in my garage. But it is repairable with a fair bit of work. It is coming home next week and I am getting stuck back into my Stage 2 bodykit with vengence. <BR>Just thought I might post a picture of some of the plans for my now t-topped soon to be convertible 86 GT.<BR>Mechanically and such there will not be a lot of Fiero left when I am done.<BR>Due to registration requirements and budget it is looking like my engine swap will probably be a fuel injected 3.5 litre alloy V8 out of a Rover. Brakes will be ABS, probably off a Holden Commodore. <BR>Inside I plant to go retro with a new dash and plenty of custom features. MOre than it currently has from the last rebuild even though 95% of the interior survived.<BR>Should look good parked next to the MR2  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroconvertible2.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero3.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||7
Z||000001||84Bill||11-27-2001||08:20 AM||||I thought I was dreaming until a coworker asked me why I was hugging my monitor  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||Nashco||11-27-2001||08:49 AM||||Those motors are sweet; most people think that all aluminum motors are something new! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I love the look of that car...doesn't it look like something completely modern?  Not many people would believe some of our cars are over a decade old!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||11-27-2001||10:29 AM||||That looks sweet AUS!  So, since you're replacing the interior... any plans to sell off the RH Drive system?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'm still interested, you know!<P>The Aluminium block motor is a great idea.  My Dad always wanted to install the 215 aluminium block V8 from an old Buick (the "grandfather" to the modern Rover engine)in a Fiero or Opel GT.  He had one completely rebuilt and was ready to go, when he pretty much decided that it was going to be too much work to relocate the starter... anyone want to buy an extra Buick 215?  We've got 3!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indy-2M4||11-27-2001||11:00 AM||||Aus, that is sweeeeet, but one thing about it....it kinda takes on the look of a 'stang on the side (on that note, I'm outta here)(as she takes off running).....really is pretty, though!<P>------------------<BR>F.K.A. KathyHL<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://sofa.iwarp.com/IndyFiero2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||11-27-2001||11:05 AM||||That looks great!<BR>It's obvious that it's a Fiero, yet it doesn't really look like one. Does that even make sense? Looks more like a Ferrari. Nice touch!<BR>Glad you're getting back on track. <P>Best,<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||11-27-2001||11:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Indy-2M4:<BR><B>Aus, that is sweeeeet, but one thing about it....it kinda takes on the look of a 'stang on the side (on that note, I'm outta here)(as she takes off running).....really is pretty, though!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nah, not really... the scoop on the stang looks like it was glued into place- much like a plastic model. Think more... C5 'vette, just faced backwards!||||reg||1
