Z||000008||WhiteFieroBlur||11-27-2001||02:33 PM||||see your hugging the monitor and I am drooling   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I love those rims. What I always wanted to know about is on the website is with the red car on the top. How is the back done like that? I don't see some kinda kit you sell to make it look like that. Where did you get that from or had that done.<p>[This message has been edited by WhiteFieroBlur (edited 11-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||AusFiero||11-27-2001||03:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by WhiteFieroBlur:<BR><B>see your hugging the monitor and I am drooling    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I love those rims. What I always wanted to know about is on the website is with the red car on the top. How is the back done like that? I don't see some kinda kit you sell to make it look like that. Where did you get that from or had that done.<P>[This message has been edited by WhiteFieroBlur (edited 11-27-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks to the fire I have not got any of Stage2 done. I have the side scoops but the panels are damaged around the edges. They are the bits, and the side skirts than I am getting stuck into first to get the huge amount of orders for them back on track.<P>The rear bar is a later addition after christmas is out of the way. I have my work space back so things will continue to be developed now. Thank god, because I have been getting sick of doing web publishing again while I have been waiting to do my car work. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||AusFiero||11-27-2001||03:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>That looks sweet AUS!  So, since you're replacing the interior... any plans to sell off the RH Drive system?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'm still interested, you know!<P>The Aluminium block motor is a great idea.  My Dad always wanted to install the 215 aluminium block V8 from an old Buick (the "grandfather" to the modern Rover engine)in a Fiero or Opel GT.  He had one completely rebuilt and was ready to go, when he pretty much decided that it was going to be too much work to relocate the starter... anyone want to buy an extra Buick 215?  We've got 3!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah the starter on that motor is a bit of a worry but worth investigating due to how cheap the motors are here. Other option may be a quad cammed alloy 4.0 litre V8 out of a Toyota. They are also cheap here.<P>The only RHD bit I wont need Minn is the dash, and it is damaged from the fire. I thought it had survived but the RH section of it is damaged. The other bits I can probably source for you if you are really that interested. The Volvo steering rack is about all you need. The rest is fabrication.<P>||||reg||1
